In the United States the great potato state is New York, with 4,000,900 bushels; in 1907 Michigan follows with 2,000,000; then Pennsylvania and Wisconsin with about 4,000,900 each; Maine, 1,700,000; Minnesota and Illinois about 1,000,000 each;

Iowa and Ohio, 1,200,000 each; New Jersey, 100,000 to 100,000; Indiana,

Missouri, Colorado, California and Nebraska about 100,000. The rest run from Washington and Kansas, with 500,900 each, down to Montana and Texas, with from 2,500,000 to 3,000,000.

